==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛnɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛnɪt|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From the same root as {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|ġerennan||to coagulate}} (compare German {{m|de|gerinnen}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*rannijaną}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# An [[enzyme]] used as the first step in making [[cheese]], to [[curdle]] the milk and [[coagulate]] the [[casein]] in it, derived by soaking the fourth [[stomach]] of a milk-fed [[calf]] in [[brine]].

=====Derived terms=====
* [[rennin]]

